---
permalink: /css/theme.css
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#-
  Template-generated theme.css. Reads from the runtime file the site-config
  plugin writes to /app/data/content/_data/theme.css (symlinked into eleventy-site
  as content/_data/theme.css). Falls back to css/theme.example.css when the
  runtime file is missing (fresh container before plugin's seed-from-env runs).

  This is THE idiomatic Eleventy pattern for serving dynamic-content-but-static
  assets (https://www.11ty.dev/docs/permalinks/). The wholesale
  addPassthroughCopy("css") in eleventy.config.js does NOT copy css/theme.css
  because that file no longer exists in the source tree (only theme.example.css
  remains); the prebuild script was updated accordingly.

  Cache invalidation: when content/_data/theme.css changes (plugin write), the
  addWatchTarget on that file triggers an Eleventy rebuild, which re-renders
  this template with the new content. The base.njk hash filter reads the same
  source, so the cache-bust query string matches the served content.
-#}
{%- set runtime = 'content/_data/theme.css' | inlineFile -%}
{%- if runtime | length > 0 -%}
{{ runtime | safe }}
{%- else -%}
{{ 'css/theme.example.css' | inlineFile | safe }}
{%- endif -%}
